<title>UK: EMU to hit bond arbitrage business hard-ISMA study.</title>
<headline>EMU to hit bond arbitrage business hard-ISMA study.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bond arbitrage business could be cut by up to 60 percent after EMU, according to an ISMA survey of 900 member firms published on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Some of the larger trading firms, say, those with a staff of 500 engaged in their bond department, have stated that the impact of the euro on their bond business could be substantial,&quot; the International Securities Market Association survey said.</p>
<p>&quot;They foresee a loss of up to 60 percent in their bond arbitrage business. These tended to be highly concentrated on intra-European bond markets&quot;.</p>
<p>ISMA is the main self-regulatory organisation for the international bond markets.</p>
<p>-- Dan Lalor, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
